-- =============================================================================
-- Metadata Sync — v1.2.x release
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Generated by `mj sync push` against a clean database built from MJ core,
-- bizapps-common (through V202608262255), and every bizapps-tasks migration
-- through V202608252210, per the release-time metadata sync ritual
-- (see V202606231615 for the v1.1.x run and bizapps-common's V202608140800
-- for the documented corrections). This file is the emitted
-- metadata/sql_logging output with core SP calls re-pointed at ${mjSchema}:
-- they exist only in __mj, and `mj migrate --schema __mj_BizAppsTasks` binds
-- flyway:defaultSchema to THIS app's schema.
--
-- WHAT THIS CARRIES — the delta between metadata/ (source of truth) and a
-- database built purely from migrations:
--   * MJ: Applications — 1 update (Tasks application record settings)
--   * MJ: Entities — 1 update (form configuration from metadata/entities/)
--   * MJ: Entity Fields — 4 updates (field pins from metadata/entities/)
--   * MJ: Entity Relationships — 22 updates (form-chrome placement from
--     metadata/entity-relationships/)
--
-- NOTE. This capture follows the removal of the form-chrome record that named
-- MJ_BizApps_Accounting: Journal Entry Batches (same commit). Tasks metadata
-- must not reference consumer apps: the @lookup cannot resolve on a database
-- without Accounting installed, and one failed lookup rolls back the entire
-- metadata push — breaking every fresh Tasks install. That record moves to
-- bizapps-accounting, which is allowed to name Tasks (dependencies point up).
-- =============================================================================

